# Static assets only.
#
# The headers that matter for a document — CSP, HSTS, frame-ancestors — are set
# on every response by src/server.ts, because that is the only place that works
# on all three supported hosts. This file covers what never reaches that code:
# files served straight off disk by Nitro's asset handler, which answers before
# the SSR entry runs.
#
# Read by Cloudflare and Netlify. A Node deployment sits behind a reverse proxy
# that has its own header configuration; see DEPLOYMENT.md.
#
# Nitro appends its own /assets/* cache rule after this block.
/*
  x-content-type-options: nosniff
  referrer-policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  x-frame-options: DENY
  cross-origin-resource-policy: same-origin
